{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["And these are the years of Yishmael's life — the Sages interpreted in Megillah: why were the years of Yishmael counted? And by the plain sense: for the honor of Avraham, since the hour of his birth was specified — and Avraham was eighty-six years old when Hagar bore Yishmael — and also the hour of his circumcision, as written: ״וישמעאל בנו בן שלש עשרה שנה וגו׳״ — so now he went back and specified all the days of his life."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:45:08.270188050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}